  "semantic_contracts": [
    "Fallback Default captures compiled Unicode identity and seven zero counters, independently owned by-value report; font-generation errors defer without incrementing fallback. Recording classifies observation, not recovery execution or successful presentation.",
    "Geometry rejection copies caller-provided owner/range/violation/work into a last-only receipt and saturates count; it neither validates supplied values nor consumes work quota. Geometry and layout-fallback counters remain independent.",
    "Session begin_frame resets reports, finish_frame publishes Copy table-work snapshot without resetting, clear clears caches only. Ready shaping diagnostics occur before current-generation admission and may precede a Deferred result; counters do not prove cache insertion or artifact presentation.",
    "Table grid/attempt, preferred/final layout calls and tracks are observed before later failures. Output is recorded after local geometry validation just before Ready; telemetry saturation/max handling is not admission or memory/resource budgeting.",
    "Actual publish macro is crate::profile_counter!, selected by any(profiling,profiling-tracy). Recorder capture_active and independent Tracy tracing branches differ; no assertion that every backend shares a capture gate. Twelve values convert to f64; publishing consumes Copy and leaves owner's report unchanged.",
    "Eight tests/40assertions are reviewed without execution. Direct-injected deferred/retired tags are not concurrent reload tests; manual phase test checks twelve values, saturation test only nine named results. No whole-workspace guard, benchmark or Cargo test execution."
  ],
